# Normalize line endings to LF on checkout for all text files.
#
# Several files are embedded into the binary at compile time via `include_str!`
# (e.g. benchmark/quality_corpus/*.json, benchmark/model_bench.sh). On a Windows
# checkout with the default `core.autocrlf=true`, those files gain CRLF line
# endings, which changes their embedded bytes — breaking content-hash tests
# (`corpus_bytes_match_pinned_sha`) and byte-exact prompt-parity tests
# (`model_bench_freeform_prompt_matches_summary_system_prompt`). Forcing `eol=lf`
# keeps the embedded bytes identical on every platform. `text=auto` lets git
# auto-detect binary files so they are left untouched.
* text=auto eol=lf
